.TH termeric 1  "termeric 0.1.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
termeric \- A GPU\-accelerated terminal emulator themed around roots and rhizomes
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtermeric\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-\-new\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-separate\-process\fR] [\fB\-\-quick\-access\fR] [\fB\-\-tab\fR] [\fB\-\-split\fR] [\fB\-\-working\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-command\fR] [\fB\-\-terminal\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-geometry\fR] [\fB\-\-app\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-renderer\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIsubcommand\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
A GPU\-accelerated terminal emulator themed around roots and rhizomes.
.PP
Options apply to the current tab or window. The first window and its first tab exist from the start; \-\-tab starts another tab in the current window, and \-\-new\-window starts another window. Everything after \-\- is the command for the current tab.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print this help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH "WINDOW GROUPING"
.TP
\fB\-\-new\-window\fR
Start another window; first, a fresh one that skips restore
.TP
\fB\-\-separate\-process\fR
Start a process of its own, even when Termeric runs
.TP
\fB\-\-quick\-access\fR
Toggle or launch one top\-edge drop\-down window
.TP
\fB\-\-tab\fR
Start another tab in the current window
.TP
\fB\-\-split\fR \fI<DIRECTION>\fR
Split the current tab after launch
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
horizontal: Add a shell pane below
.IP \(bu 2
vertical: Add a shell pane to the right
.RE
.SH "LAUNCH SELECTION"
.TP
\fB\-\-working\-directory\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Start the current tab in PATH [alias: \-\-cwd]
.TP
\fB\-\-command\fR \fI<PROGRAM>\fR
Run PROGRAM directly, without arguments
.TP
\fB\-\-terminal\-profile\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Launch a configured terminal profile
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<AGENT:PROFILE>\fR
Launch a coding agent with a named profile
.TP
\fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Restore one complete workspace into this window
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
Set the current tab title
.TP
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
Run COMMAND in the current tab with every remaining argument exactly
.SH "NATIVE IDENTITY AND SIZE"
.TP
\fB\-\-geometry\fR \fI<WIDTHxHEIGHT>\fR
Initial physical\-pixel window size
.TP
\fB\-\-app\-id\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Set the X11 WM_CLASS and Wayland application ID [alias: \-\-class]
.SH RENDERING
.TP
\fB\-\-renderer\fR \fI<BACKEND>\fR
Choose the renderer for every window of this process
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Try the GPU, then software rendering
.IP \(bu 2
gpu: Insist on the GPU
.IP \(bu 2
software: Insist on software rendering
.RE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\fBtermeric domain\fR
Keep terminals running in a background daemon, here or over SSH (experimental). Run \fBtermeric domain \-\-help\fR for its commands and options.
.TP
\fBtermeric control\fR
Script the windows, tabs, and panes of a running Termeric (experimental). Run \fBtermeric control \-\-help\fR for its commands and options.
.TP
\fBtermeric plugin\fR
Install and manage plugins (experimental). Run \fBtermeric plugin \-\-help\fR for its commands and options.
.TP
\fBtermeric workspace\fR
List saved workspaces. Run \fBtermeric workspace \-\-help\fR for its commands and options.
.TP
\fBtermeric mcp\fR
Serve Termeric\*(Aqs agent tools to a coding agent over MCP (experimental). Run \fBtermeric mcp \-\-help\fR for its commands and options.
.SH "JOINING A RUNNING TERMERIC"
A plain launch opens its window in the Termeric already running on this display, so tabs can move between its windows; the window uses that process\*(Aqs settings and environment. A launch starts a process of its own instead when it passes \-\-separate\-process, opens two or more windows, or uses any option besides \-\-new\-window, \-\-tab, \-\-working\-directory, \-\-title, \-\-command, and a COMMAND; when [window] share_process is false; when the termeric executable differs from the running one; when any of these variables differs from the running process\*(Aqs: RUST_LOG, WGPU_BACKEND, WGPU_ADAPTER_NAME, WGPU_POWER_PREF, LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE, HOME, XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME; or when TERMERIC_TERM, TERMERIC_TERMINFO_DIR, TERMINFO, and TERMINFO_DIRS select a different terminal identity (TERM and its terminfo entry) from the running process\*(Aqs.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBTERMERIC_TERM\fR
The TERM programs in Termeric see: auto (the default) uses xterm\-termeric when its terminfo entry is installed and xterm\-256color otherwise; xterm\-256color (or compatibility) always uses xterm\-256color; xterm\-termeric insists on Termeric\*(Aqs own entry and falls back with a logged warning.
.TP
\fBTERMERIC_TERMINFO_DIR\fR
A directory searched first for the compiled xterm\-termeric entry, before TERMINFO, ~/.terminfo, $XDG_DATA_HOME/terminfo, TERMINFO_DIRS, the install prefix\*(Aqs share/terminfo, and the system directories.
.TP
\fBWGPU_BACKEND\fR
The graphics API to render with: vulkan or gl. With \-\-renderer software, gl and LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=true use Mesa\*(Aqs software OpenGL.
.TP
\fBRUST_LOG\fR
What Termeric logs to standard error, for example warn,termeric=debug.
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME\fR
Where Termeric keeps its configuration (termeric/config.toml, custom themes, plugins) and its data (workspaces, tab snapshots, agent transcripts), by default ~/.config and ~/.local/share.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/.config/termeric/config.toml\fR
The configuration, reloaded when it is saved. config.example.toml, in Termeric\*(Aqs documentation directory (such as /usr/share/doc/termeric), lists every setting with its default.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
The project, with its README and plugin examples: https://github.com/Tjemmmic/termeric
